      <div type="clause" n="90.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 90.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 90.2" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="605" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="e" target="#Hn_90-2.lnote.oe.e"/> quis arcu uel balista desubitanti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="f" target="#Hn_90-2.lnote.oe.f"/> uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Hn_90-2.lnote.oe.30"/> pedico ad lupos uel (ad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Hn_90-2.lnote.oe.31"/>) aliud capiendum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Hn_90-2.lnote.oe.32"/> posito dampnum uel malum aliquod recipiat, soluat qui posuit.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 605 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_90-2.lnote.oe.e" n="e" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">605</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. ebd.</hi> VIII 4, 23: Si quis … arcos protenderit seu ballistas …; <hi rend="italic">Lex Burgund.</hi> 46: Quicunque occidendorum luporum studio arcus posuerint …; <hi rend="italic">ebd.</hi> 72: Si quis pedicam feris fecerit …; <hi rend="italic">ferner Lex Sax.</hi> 56; <hi rend="italic">Angl. Wer.</hi> 61. <hi rend="italic">Aber Nebenumstände und Entscheidungen variiren: also Benutzung durch Hn unwahrscheinlich</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. ibid. VIII 4, 23: Si quis … arcos protenderit seu ballistas …; Lex Burgund. 46: Quicunque occidendorum luporum studio arcus posuerint …; ibid. 72: Si quis pedicam feris fecerit …; further Lex Sax. 56; Angl. Wer. 61. But the attendant circumstances and the decisions vary: use of these by Hn is therefore improbable</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_90-2.lnote.oe.f" n="f" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">605</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">auf <hi rend="italic">den Menschen</hi> fallend; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Quadr. Af 23</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">falling upon the person; cf. Quadr. Af 23</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_90-2.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">605</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u. p. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u. p. missing Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_90-2.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">605</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nicht in Sc Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not in Sc Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_90-2.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">605</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K Co Or Gi</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in K Co Or Gi</seg></note>
      </div>
